Arithmetic field families and planar unit distances

New formalization code, proof development and documentation were produced by
Codex under Eric Naslund's direction, September 2026. Earlier proof work used
GPT-6 Astra with Ultra reasoning; the September 24 selected-tree migration
was led by GPT-6 Sol with a GPT-6 Astra Ultra specialist, two GPT-6 Sol
collaborators and GPT-6 Luna collaborators. The source mathematics is Eric
Naslund's manuscript
"A lower exponent of 1.0418235 for planar unit distances", research commit
eec70fd25ebe045c5df1c98370d613eaa3719c0c. This is a partial, conditional
formalization; it does not prove the manuscript's complete main theorem.

